Goal: for bounded measurable f (pointwise bound ∀y, ‖f y‖ ≤ M, 0 ≤ M), x ↦ P_t f x is C¹, with derivative at x₀ equal to ∫ y, (fderiv of x ↦ K(x - y) at x₀) (f y) dy.

Using `hasFDerivAt_integral_of_dominated_of_fderiv_le`:
```
{F : H → α → E} {F' : H → α → H →L[𝕜] E} (hs : s ∈ 𝓝 x₀)
    (hF_meas : ∀ᶠ x in 𝓝 x₀, AEStronglyMeasurable (F x) μ)
    (hF_int : Integrable (F x₀) μ)
    (hF'_meas : AEStronglyMeasurable (F' x₀) μ)
    (h_bound : ∀ᵐ a ∂μ, ∀ x ∈ s, ‖F' x a‖ ≤ bound a)
    (bound_integrable : Integrable (bound : α → ℝ) μ)
    (h_diff : ∀ᵐ a ∂μ, ∀ x ∈ s, HasFDerivAt (F · a) (F' x a) x) :
    HasFDerivAt (fun x ↦ ∫ a, F x a ∂μ) (∫ a, F' x₀ a ∂μ) x₀
```

Here H = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n), α = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) (integration variable y), E = ℝ, 𝕜 = ℝ.

F x y := gaussianKernel n t (x - y) * f y
F' x y := fderiv ℝ (fun z => gaussianKernel n t (z - y) * f y) x = fderiv (fun z => gaussianKernel n t (z - y)) x • f y — since the multiplier f y is constant in x: fderiv of z ↦ K(z-y)·f y = (fderiv (z ↦ K(z-y)) x).smulRight... for E = ℝ scalar field: the linear map is (fun v => fderiv K(x-y) v * f y) — hmm — the multiplication by f y: z ↦ K(z-y)·f y = mul with f y ∘ (z ↦ K(z-y)) — derivative = f y • fderiv (z ↦ K(z-y)) x. As a continuous linear map: (fderiv (z ↦ K(z-y)) x).smulRight (f y)? The map v ↦ (fderiv K v) * (f y) = (fderiv K).smulRight (f y). 

Compute fderiv of z ↦ K(z - y) at x: K(z-y) = (4πt)^{-n/2} exp(-‖z-y‖²/(4t)) — derivative = K(x-y) * (inner (y - x) / (2t))·: fderiv = (fun v => gaussianKernel n t (x - y) * (⟪y - x, v⟫ / (2*t))) — i.e. gradient = K(x-y)·(y-x)/(2t).

